---
description: Ball Takes frontend product and visual rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- Preserve the core loop: Discover -> Follow pundits -> Predict -> Compare -> Receipt -> Banter -> Studio -> Export.
- Studio is a primary destination. Never remove or demote it without explicit instruction.
- Pundit comparison and receipts are core differentiators.
- Prefer existing design primitives and dependencies before adding new ones.
- Every async UI touched must handle loading, loaded, empty, stale and error states.
- Never render a blank section for a failed data dependency.
- Never fabricate pundit quotes, football facts, production feed content or engagement metrics.
- Keep the application shell restrained; derive visual energy from football context, media, receipts and state changes.
- Ball Takes green is an accent/action/status color, not a default background for everything.
- Avoid gratuitous gradients, glow, glassmorphism, oversized radii and perpetual animation.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion and visible keyboard focus.
- Do not weaken or bypass GDPR consent, CAPTCHA, bot checks, WAF or other security controls.
- Ad placements must not disrupt prediction controls or split a receipt comparison; collapse unavailable/non-consented slots.
